  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One save; optional event",
      "items": [
        "The entity and outbox row commit in the same save when messaging is enabled",
        "The event is raised by the save hook, never sent from application code"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "What this can't show",
      "items": [
        "The transaction boundary is the one SaveChanges call: entity and enabled outbox row commit together or not at all",
        "A group holds accounts only by reference (GroupId) — never a mapped EF Core relationship"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Checks and outcomes",
      "items": [
        "code free: Otherwise refused: 422 DUPLICATE_GROUP_CODE, before the handler runs",
        "insert AccountGroup + outbox row, one save: new AccountGroup(code, name, description, type, ownerId, metadata), Status = Active. SlimBus EF Core interceptor auto-saves after the handler returns.",
        "account-groups.created event: Dropped, not stored, if the bus is off. Retried indefinitely from the outbox if the bus is on but unreachable."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Validation precedes creation",
      "items": [
        "The duplicate-code lookup runs in the request validator before the generated create handler"
      ]
    }
  ]
